  "unresolved": [
    "No screen recording of the scroll-reveal, count-up and bar-fill motion was made. Motion was verified through computed transform values and reduced-motion captures; the captures themselves use the reduced-motion render so headless frames cannot freeze a reveal at partial opacity.",
    "The no-flash guarantee is structural (the theme script precedes the stylesheet and the first frame is checked for the correct body background), not a frame-by-frame recording of a cold load.",
    "The skip-link reveal and its focus ring were not visually confirmed in the headless preview because document focus and transition frames did not apply. The CSS :focus-visible rule and .skip-link:focus rule are present.",
    "In the dev-only worst-case comparison, the deliberately long capability label compresses the first table column at 390 px. It remains readable and scrollable; a fixed first-column width is the recommended follow-up if this data shape ever becomes public."
  ]
